what The build receipt's hit path now spends about 112 ms of a 140 ms reading walking rye/lib/std, reading all 552 files and 16,416,628 bytes and hashing them in software -- roughly 80 percent of the work of proving a skip is safe, spent on a tree nobody touched. Measured here with the current binary: a warm hit is 140-146 ms, a walk-and-stat-only pass over the same tree is 16-21 ms including process start, and hashing its bytes alone is 145-154 ms. One stat cannot stand for a tree, so compose the tree's identity from the walk: hash the sorted relative path, size, inode, mtime and ctime of every file into one identity digest, remember the content digest beside the rye binary under that identity in a Kyri record, and feed the remembered 32 bytes into the key while inode, size, mtime, ctime and tree membership all still agree. The walk stays and the read goes; ryekey_marker moves v8 to v9 because the key absorbs a digest where it absorbed a byte stream.
