what docs-geode/demos/README.md hands a newcomer five commands and prints what each answered, and nothing in this tree runs one of them. tools/d/docs_command_path_witness.rish proves a printed PATH resolves; no instrument proves a printed OUTPUT still holds. Two of the five blocks are fixed-input answers that must never move -- the resolver's three lines and a SHA3-256 digest of five bytes -- and two more declare themselves volatile in an HTML comment that nothing reads. Run the page against itself: parse each sh fence and the output fence below it, run the command from the repository root, compare, and report matched | drifted | skipped-volatile. Roster the page rather than the room, because running what a page prints is a capability that wants a named list.
